; ============================================================================
; wpms_housekeeping_dispatch.pfasm — the housekeeping window of the Phase 3
; score in its R1 dispatch form (hw/l2/scores/wpms_r1d.score).
;
; BCP first, exactly as wpms_housekeeping.pfasm (Deliverable 3 §6.2). Then the
; window prepares the next sweep's entry: it reads the status view (Map v0.3
; §4: [8] HK phase = 1, [7:4] P of SWEEP.a — the word BCP has just landed —,
; [3:0] q = 0 in HK) and writes JumpVal = TAIL_BASE + 16·P, the address of the
; housekeeping tail that ends in the queued Jump to SLEEP_P. The score's
; background indirect Jump (JumpInd) reads JumpVal right after WJV: a
; background computed dispatch, the use Register Map v0.3 §2 allows JumpVal
; (W-T3 restricts only the foreground).
;
; TAIL_BASE = 0x300 in wpms_r1d.score:  ADD #(0x300 - 0x100) = ADD #512.
; A Layer 3 program of this build; the golden oracle keeps running the
; one-instruction wpms_housekeeping.pfasm, whose effect on the store and on
; SWEEP.a this program shares (the rest writes Accm, ADRS and JumpVal only).
; License: MIT (Layer 3). Illustrative.
; ============================================================================
.window wpms_housekeeping_dispatch
.bg
        BCP                     ; W-F27: land the take-set; SWEEP.a <- sweep item
        SAD     0x11A           ; status view
        LDA     @PPM            ; Accm = 0x100 + 16 P   (HK, q = 0)
        ADD     #512            ; Accm = 0x300 + 16 P = TAIL_P
        WJV                     ; JumpVal <- Accm[11:0]
